// Sliding window (fixed size): max sum of any k consecutive elements
public static int maxSumOfK(int[] arr, int k) {
    int windowSum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) windowSum += arr[i];     // first window
    int maxSum = windowSum;
    for (int i = k; i < arr.length; i++) {
        windowSum += arr[i] - arr[i - k];                // add entering, remove leaving
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);
    }
    return maxSum;
}

// arr = {2,1,5,1,3,2}, k = 3 -> 9 (the window [5,1,3])
```
Variable-size problems reuse the same idea with two pointers: a `right` that expands and a `left` that contracts when the window breaks a rule.

